{"name":"I Miss You","hex":"#dddbc5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"miss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fail to hit, catch, grasp, etc.","To avoid hitting."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A failure to physically hit.","A failure to obtain or accomplish something; a failure to succeed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miss"},{"term":"you","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Pronoun","definitions":["The people spoken, or written to, as an object. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","(To) yourselves, (to) yourself."]},{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["The individual or group spoken or written to.","Used before epithets, describing the person being addressed, for emphasis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/you"}],"entries":[{"title":"I Miss You (1992 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Anueng Khitthueng Pho Sangkhep, later released with the English title I Miss You, is a 1992 Thai coming-of-age film directed by Bhandit Rittakol and released by Five Star Production. The story follows a group of upper-secondary school students in Chiang Mai, and launched the careers of several of its actors, including Ann Thongprasom, Katreeya English, Saitharn Niyomkarn, members of the boy band Boyscout, and Juckkrit Amarat. The film was a commercial success and helped spark a wave of Thai teen films that followed in the 1990s. The film was shot at Yupparaj Wittayalai School."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Miss_You_(1992_film)","wikidata":"Q13023609"},{"title":"I Miss You (2011 film)","blocks":[{"text":"I Miss You is a Swedish drama film directed by Anders Grönros and based on the 1992 young adult novel I Miss You, I Miss You! by Kinna Gieth and Peter Pohl. The film was released in 2011."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Miss_You_(2011_film)","wikidata":"Q10539097"},{"title":"I Miss You (Blink-182 song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"I Miss You\" is a song by the American rock band Blink-182. It was released as the second single from the group's self-titled album (2003) on February 2, 2004, through Geffen Records. An emo and alternative rock song, it was written by guitarist Tom DeLonge, bassist Mark Hoppus, and drummer Travis Barker, and was produced by Jerry Finn. The track marks a stylistic departure for the band, built around acoustic instrumentation including stand-up bass, cello, piano, and a brushstroked drum loop, layered into a moody, groove-driven arrangement. Its gothic style was inspired by the Cure."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9d/Blink-182_-_I_Miss_You_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Miss_You_(Blink-182_song)","wikidata":"Q2739062"},{"title":"I","blocks":[{"text":"I is the ninth letter and the third vowel letter of the Latin alphabet, used in the modern English alphabet, the alphabets of other western European languages and others worldwide. Its name in English is i, plural i's or is."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Latin_letter_I.svg/330px-Latin_letter_I.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I","wikidata":"Q9893"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/Jonas_Akerlund.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/Jonas_Akerlund.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The music video of \"I Miss You\" was directed by Jonas Åkerlund (pictured).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJonas_Akerlund.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/The_Letter_%22i%22_in_Different_European_Languages.png/500px-The_Letter_%22i%22_in_Different_European_Languages.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u